以当木棍来抵挡几下。唐小虾见她进来就不再发呆了，很自然的往另一边挪了挪给她留出了坐的地方，仿佛两人的关系已经亲到不用问的地步了。这要是在现代，洛思琦是绝不肯这么轻易的坐到一个男生旁边的，何况这个男生和她才认识不到两天。不过这次洛思琦没有任何抵触情绪的坐了过去，她觉得自己这次并不是违反了她之前的原则，而是情况特殊，不得不。她问唐小虾：“唐小虾，你刚才究竟是什么意思？”唐小虾苦笑了一下，对她说：“你别问了，就当我当时什么都没说，好不好？”洛思琪尽管不是一个胡搅蛮缠的女生，可也不想就这么算了。就在洛思琦刚想说什么的时候，唐小虾却突然做出了一个嘘声的动作，然后到门前听了听，便回来对她说：“小心隔墙有耳，咱小些声说。”唐小虾的举动让洛思琪很惊讶，她狐疑的看着唐小虾，见他目光坚决，便只好小声的问他：“怎么了？”唐小虾挠了挠头，轻声说：“不知道为什么，总觉得我们现在的处境不太妙！”“怎么不妙了？伍家和咱们同行的有十几个人，不管是饮食起居还是寻人引路，都不用咱们操心，况且这里应该离楚都尚远，哪里有什么不妙啦！“洛思琪觉得唐小虾的感觉很奇怪，便这样问他。唐小虾的回答差点让洛思琪伸手去打他，因为他的回答只是说：“不妙，不妙，就是不妙，我们现在应该立刻带上行囊和钱立刻离开这里。”洛思琦很想把她的小手放在唐小虾的额头上问他有没有发烧，还是出来因为水土不服得了什么妄想症！就在这个时候，客栈楼下却来了一群不速之客，这群不速之客还是一大群！洛思琪听到吵嚷声便想出去看看，却被唐小虾急忙拉住了，两人将门微微的开了一些，小心翼翼的向楼下看去。他们见到客栈老板惊慌的迎了出去，见了领头便更慌张了，他对那一身军装打扮的人连连作揖到：“城守大人您怎么亲自来了，这么大排场是要抓谁啊？”那城守看都不看他一眼，指挥士兵封锁了门口到楼梯的通道，直接就带人向楼上走来。洛思琪和唐小虾也不知道这些人上来就抓谁的，却还是赶紧把门关上了，心想多一事不如少一事！可就在这时，隔壁却忽然乒乒乓乓的打起来了。洛思琦住在唐小虾屋子的右边，左边的几个房间都是伍家那十几个人住的，而声音正是从左边传出来的。两人可以听出伍家人和来抓人的康城城守打的很凶，不停都东西被撞倒花瓶被碰到地上摔碎的声音！“怎么办？怎么办？”洛思琦看向唐小虾，发现唐小虾的表情急剧变化，似乎正在想解决的办法，唐小虾突然对她说：“我们两个人的能力你也知道，就算我们两个人冲过去也肯定打不过那么多人，我们贸贸然去冲过去，不但帮不上忙，说不定还会给人家添麻烦，我们还是老实呆着，静观其变吧！”洛思琦觉得这样袖手旁观很是不好，但她在雪云谷这些天练剑还不如唐小虾勤奋，倒是总召唤出水来结冰玩了。她只好同意唐小虾说的，不过心中还是有些过意不去，毕竟伍家的人虽说跟她基本没有关系，但现在怎么也算一伙儿的啊！她看了看手中的披雪剑，站起来，却还是又坐了回去。外面的声音越来越大，听声音好像已经打到楼下了，可慢慢还是逐渐停止了，洛思琦听到楼下把人押走的声音，似乎伍家的人还是跑掉了一个，引起别人去追。等到楼下只剩下客栈老板的抱怨声和小二们收拾桌椅板凳的声音时，洛思琦才看到唐小虾去开了门。唐小虾很快就回来了，他对洛思琦说：“客栈老板说来的人是康城城守，前来缉拿伍家的人，打伤抓住了十几个，没有死人，却跑掉一个，听他的描述似乎是伍绪！”洛思琦没想到他们刚出来就突遭变故，不光领头的伍绪逃跑了生死未定，其余和她一起来的伍家人也都纷纷被抓了，现在只剩下她和唐小虾，人生地不熟的，还怎么去楚都救人啊！好在有唐小虾在，他快速的帮洛思琦做了反应，他二话不说拿起行囊就将洛思琦拉出了房间，对她说：“不管怎样，此地不宜久留，你取把你的行囊也取出来，我们赶紧换一个地方！”好在两个人出来匆忙，除了放着钱的行囊和手中的剑都没有带别的东西，他们急匆匆又加倍小心的离开了客栈，掌柜的看他们的样子都是哆哆嗦嗦的，也敢阻拦，洛思琪在唐小虾的带领下东拐西拐的找到了一家偏僻一点的小客栈，这小客栈连名字都没有，只有一层，只是挂着能看出是客栈的小牌子，唐小虾付了二个银布币做房钱，只要了一间房。开一间房的时候洛思琪只来得及说了一个字：“这——”便被唐小虾一句：“两人一起安全！”给说的不说话了。整个过程洛思琦没再提出异议，直到进了房间，她才问唐小虾两个人一间房可怎么住？唐小虾不出意料的指了指房间内的木桌子对洛思琦说“我睡桌子，你睡床！”按理说就是该这样的，洛思琦想到也许唐小虾在进了永宁客栈后说两人住一个房间可能就是这个想法，不禁稍稍有点安心，尽管她也不能保证唐小虾不会在晚上趁她睡着的时候偷偷摸上床来，但在这种只有彼此还算相识的危机下，她觉得自己还是可以相信唐小虾的，如果在这个充满未知和危机的时候他还有闲心想别的，那他可真不是个人了！躺在床上的洛思琦稍稍松了一口气，她看唐小虾坐在桌边趴在上面休息有点不忍，可毕竟也不能提出来让他到床上来，便头冲向他看着他，心想：“他也只有十七岁啊，可自己也没什么主意，接下来要怎么办，还得靠他啊！”店家过了一会儿送来了两大碗米饭和几个菜，洛思琦还真有些饿了，她坐到桌子前看到唐小虾盯着饭菜许久没动，不禁催促道：“看着干什么啊？快吃啊？”她看到唐小虾对她摆了摆手说：“等一等，我还有点事想不明白。”", "source": "www.quanwenyuedu.io", "source_url": "https://www.quanwenyuedu.io/n/laidaochunqiudangyueshen/10.html", "_fixed": true, "content_en": "Chapter 9 Incidents and Updates Although she and Tang Xiaoxia lived in two rooms at Luo Siqi's insistence, and when Luo Siqi found out that only four people in the Wu family lived in one room, she felt it was a bit extravagant, but men and women were not intimate, and even now she felt that Tang Xiaoxia would not be able to live in the same room with him no matter how close they were! Besides, there is only one bed in the room. Luo Siqi was very curious as to why the four people from the Wu family only shared one room. This bed could only sleep two people at most, and the four of them were so strong. How could they squeeze into one bed? Luo Siqi didn't believe that they were trying to save money, but she didn't have the heart to find out the detailed reasons. After resting in the room for a while, she couldn't help but go out and push Tang Xiaoxia's door open. She wanted to ask Tang Xiaoxia which part was wrong and why he wanted to share a room with her. Tang Xiaoxia's door was unlocked. She closed the door after entering and saw Tang Xiaoxia sitting on the bed in a daze, with his Lingyun Sword placed on the bedside. In fact, Luo Siqi also came with the Pixue Sword. Although she almost couldn't use it, she felt that having a sword was always better than not having one. When in danger, she didn't know how to use it and could use it as a stick to resist a few blows. When Tang Xiaoxia saw her coming in, he stopped being in a daze and naturally moved to the other side to leave a place for her to sit, as if the relationship between the two was so close that there was no need to ask. In modern times, Luo Siqi would never sit next to a boy so easily, not to mention that the boy had only known her for less than two days. But this time Luo Siqi sat over without any resistance. She felt that she had not violated her previous principles this time, but that the situation was special and she had to. She asked Tang Xiaoxia: \"Tang Xiaoxia, what did you mean just now?\" Tang Xiaoxia smiled bitterly and said to her: \"Stop asking, just pretend I didn't say anything at that time, okay?\" Although Luo Siqi was not a messy girl, she didn't want to let it go. Just when Luo Siqi was about to say something, Tang Xiaoxia suddenly made a hissing gesture, then went to the door to listen, and then came back and said to her: \"Be careful, the walls have ears. Let's speak in a lower voice.\" Tang Xiaoxia's behavior surprised Luo Siqi. She looked at Tang Xiaoxia suspiciously, and when she saw his firm gaze, she had to ask him in a low voice: \"What's wrong?\" Tang Xiaoxia scratched his head. He raised his head and said softly: \"I don't know why, but I always feel that our current situation is not good!\" \"Why is it not good? There are more than a dozen people from the Wu family traveling with us. We don't need to worry about food, daily life, or finding people to guide us. Besides, this place should be far away from Chudu, so there is nothing wrong with it!\" Luo Siqi felt that Tang Xiaoxia felt strange, so she asked him. Tang Xiaoxia's answer almost made Luo Siqi reach out to hit him, because his answer just said: \"It's not good, it's not good, it's just not good. We should take our bags and money and leave here immediately.\" Luo Siqi wanted to put her little hand on Tang Xiaoxia's forehead and ask him if he had a fever, or was she suffering from some delusional disorder due to acclimatization! At this time, a group of uninvited guests came downstairs of the inn. This group of uninvited guests was still a large group! When Luo Siqi heard the noise, she wanted to go out and take a look, but Tang Xiaoxia hurriedly stopped her. The two of them opened the door slightly and looked downstairs cautiously. When they saw the innkeeper, they rushed out in panic. When they saw the leader, they became even more panicked. He bowed to the man in military uniform and said, \"Why are you here in person, Lord City Guard? Who are you trying to arrest in such a grand ceremony?\" The city guard didn't even look at him, and ordered the soldiers to block the passage from the door to the stairs, and led the people directly upstairs. Luo Siqi and Tang Xiaoxia didn't know who these people were going to catch, but they still quickly closed the door, thinking that it would be better to do less than to do more! But at this moment, there suddenly started a ping-pong-pong fight next door. Luo Siqi lived on the right side of Tang Xiaoxia's house. The rooms on the left were occupied by the dozen or so people from the Wu family, and the sound came from the left. The two of them could hear the dewu family and the Kangcheng City Guards who came to arrest people were beating fiercely. Things were being knocked over and vases were being hit and broken on the ground! \"What to do? What to do?\" Luo Siqi looked at Tang Xiaoxia and found that Tang Xiaoxia's expression changed drastically. He seemed to be thinking of a solution. Tang Xiaoxia suddenly said to her: \"You also know the abilities of the two of us. Even if the two of us rush over, we will definitely not be able to defeat so many people. We trade If you rush over hastily, not only will you not be able to help, but you may also cause trouble for others. We should just stay calm and wait and see what happens!\" Luo Siqi felt that it was not good to stand by and do nothing like this, but she was not as diligent as Tang Xiaoxia in practicing swordsmanship in Xueyun Valley these days, and she always summoned water to freeze and play. She had no choice but to agree with what Tang Xiaoxia said, but she still felt a little regretful. After all, although the Wu family had basically nothing to do with her, they were still considered a group now! She looked at the snow-covered sword in her hand, stood up, but sat back down. The sound outside became louder and louder. It seemed that the sound had reached downstairs, but it gradually stopped. Luo Siqi heard the sound of people being taken away downstairs. It seemed that one of the Wu family members had escaped, causing others to chase them. When the only sounds downstairs were the innkeeper's complaints and the waiters clearing tables, chairs and benches, Luo Siqi saw Tang Xiaoxia open the door. Tang Xiaoxia came back soon. He said to Luo Siqi: \"The innkeeper said that the person who came here was the city guard of Kangcheng. He came to arrest the Wu family. He wounded and arrested more than a dozen people. No one died, but one escaped. From his description, it seems to be Wu Xu!\" Luo Siqi! Unexpectedly, something unexpected happened to them as soon as they came out. Not only Wu Xu, the leader, escaped and his life and death were uncertain, but the rest of the Wu family members who came with her were also arrested one after another. Now only she and Tang Xiaoxia were left. They were unfamiliar with the place. How could they go to Chudu to save people! Fortunately, Tang Xiaoxia was there and he quickly helped Luo Si.", "title_en": "Chapter 10"}